---
// Full-bleed band whose left edge is cut by a PERFECT CIRCLE — never an ellipse,
// at any viewport size.
//
// LAYERING (this is what makes the circle possible):
//   1. The section's base colour is RED.
//   2. An orange strip, bounded, on the left.
//   3. The red circle on top of it. Its left arc is the curve.
// Everything to the right of the strip is already red, so the circle NEVER has
// to span the viewport. That is the whole trick: an orange base would force the
// circle to be wide enough to cover the widest screen, and a circle wide enough
// for a 2560px monitor cuts an almost flat arc across a ~600px band (measured:
// 25px of sweep instead of 68px). Decoupling the fill from the shape buys back
// the curve. The strip is capped in px so the circle always covers it, however
// wide the screen gets.
//
// SIZING — aspect-square + rounded-full, driven by the band's HEIGHT:
//   sweep / band height = (r/2) x (1 - sqrt(1 - 1/r^2))
// which depends ONLY on the ratio r, not on the viewport. So the arc keeps the
// same proportion to the band at every screen size — measured 13.4% of the band
// height at r=2 and 5% at r=5, identically at 500px and at 2560px wide.
// Sizing the circle in vw instead would make it flatten on wide screens and
// bulge on narrow ones.
//
// Mobile uses a bigger circle (flatter arc) on purpose: at r=2 the arc would eat
// ~80px, and a 375px screen cannot pay for both that and a readable text column.
// It is still a perfect circle — only its radius differs.
//
// Content padding must clear the arc's WIDEST intrusion (its position at the
// band's top and bottom edges), never its midpoint.
---

<section class="relative w-full overflow-hidden bg-brand text-white">
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-[40%] max-w-[520px] bg-brand-orange"
  >
  </div>

  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute top-1/2 left-4 aspect-square h-[500%] -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-brand md:left-[5%] md:h-[200%]"
  >
  </div>

  <div
    class="relative z-10 flex flex-col gap-28 py-24 pr-5 pl-16 md:gap-44 md:py-36 md:pr-[6%] md:pl-[22%]"
  >
    <slot />
  </div>
</section>
